Important Concept:

Two Way Data Binding [(ngModel)]:
 -- refers to synchronization or sharing of the data between the model(the component) and the view(Html template).
 -- It allows the automatic update of both  the model and the view when either one changes. 
 -- Two binding is a combination of propeerty binding and event binding
   [(ngModel)]="dynamicInput" <=> 
                   [ngModel]="modelProperty"                //property binding
                   (ngModelChange)= "modelProperty=$event"  //event binding

To make two way binding possible, first need to import FromsModule, because it has ngModel directive in template driven 
forms 
It controls and handles-input,textarea, select etc.,

*One way binding is simpler and two way binding privides real time synchronization between model and the view.

Note: Simple cart example can also done by using get method for total price and readOnly property in html.

